      "description" : {
         "content" : [
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "qContainersPrivateSyncrhonizationPolicy_    qContainersPrivateSyncrhonizationPolicy_DebugExternalSyncMutex_",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "BIG performance imporvement if possible",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "I THINK it is.",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "We now externally syncronize the CONTAINER. And the date is only mutated if the connection count = 1.",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "My first test failed - but I suspect thats just because of updating the iteraotrs (which still MUST be synchonized even if all readonly).",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            },
            {
               "content" : [
                  {
                     "text" : "So - break aprart macros/logic so sep macro for updating iterator linked list. THEN - I think we may be abel to get this to work. And that updating iterator linked list CAN use non-recursive mutex or even spinlcok since lifetime definitlely very short.",
                     "type" : "text"
                  }
               ],
               "type" : "paragraph"
            }
         ],
         "type" : "doc",
         "version" : 1
      },
